sequenceDiagram
    participant W as Worker (Phase 2)
    participant O as Orchestrator
    participant K as Kafka
    participant E as External System
    participant DB as DTM Database

    Note over W,E: Step 1: Worker completes processing and calls back

    W->>O: POST /callback (success + output data)
    O->>DB: Update step → COMPLETED
    O->>O: Check cascade config for this cascade

    alt Cascade has no FK dependencies (root cascade)
        O->>K: Publish to cascade.completed topic
        O->>DB: Update step → WAITING_FOR_ACK
        Note over O,K: Data flows immediately
    else Cascade depends on parent (has fkFields)
        O->>DB: Store output data
        O->>O: Check: do all parent ACKs exist?
        alt All parent ACKs received
            O->>O: Inject FK values from parent ACKs into payload
            O->>K: Publish enriched data to cascade.completed topic
            O->>DB: Update step → WAITING_FOR_ACK
        else Waiting for parent ACKs
            O->>DB: Mark as cascade-pending
            Note over O,DB: Will retry when parent ACK arrives
        end
    end

    Note over K,E: Step 2: External system processes data

    K->>E: cascade.completed message
    E->>E: Process data, generate primary key

    Note over E,O: Step 3: External system sends ACK

    E->>K: cascade.ack message (with primary key)
    K->>O: ACK handler receives message
    O->>DB: Store ACK data (primary key, payload)
    O->>DB: Update step → COMPLETED (from WAITING_FOR_ACK)

    Note over O,DB: Step 4: Cascade trigger check

    O->>O: Check: do any dependent cascades depend on this ACK?
    alt Dependent cascades waiting on this FK
        O->>O: Inject FK (parent primary key) into dependent payload
        O->>K: Publish dependent cascade data to cascade.completed topic
        O->>DB: Update dependent step → WAITING_FOR_ACK
    end

    O->>O: continueJob() — check if more steps can run
